+## 6. The descriptor-only host profile
+
+`board.target: host` (#983) describes an end station this repository builds
+no gateware for. It is a board that runs the split placement's control
+firmware as a host program on the mailbox model
+([`sw/firmware/ctrl/host/mbx_model.c`](../sw/firmware/ctrl/host/mbx_model.c)),
+and its gPTP owner is that board's own PHC. The annotated example is
+[`configs/host/endstation_host_example.yaml`](../configs/host/endstation_host_example.yaml).
+It carries #983's first stream inventory: one 8-channel AAF input, the CRF
+input an AAF talker requires (Milan v1.2 7.2.2) and one 8-channel AAF output.
+It has no CRF output, because it has no second AAF input (7.2.3). ADP
+advertises one source and two sinks.
+
+**What it feeds.** The same generators an FPGA config feeds:
+`emit_aem_overlay`, the AEM image (`_entity_model_image`, the protocol
+processor's packer and its model lint), and the firmware's
+[`adp_entity.py`](../sw/firmware/ctrl/adp/adp_entity.py) (the ADP fields),
+[`aecp_entity.py`](../sw/firmware/ctrl/aecp/aecp_entity.py) (the image AECP
+serves, its CRC and its storage sizes) and
+[`srp_entity.py`](../sw/firmware/ctrl/srp/srp_entity.py) (the shape header).
+`build()` refuses the profile by name: it writes no SoC argv, sweep fragment,
+shape include, lwSRP table or gPTP microcode for it.
+
+**What is unchanged.** Every entity, clocking, names, stream, format, SRP,
+platform, cluster-layout and model-id check of section 3 runs on it, in the
+same functions and with the same words. That includes the Milan v1.2 7.2.3
+CRF output rule, the 5.3.3.6 INTERNAL source rule, the 5.3.3.4 format and
+buffer rules, 6.4's derived format family, the 5.3.3.9 dynamic input maps,
+the 802.1AS-2011 8.1 domain rule, the IEEE 1588-2008 Table 6 clockAccuracy
+values, SRP's class A ceiling and the reserved model ids. The FPGA targets
+keep every check they had. The one addition is row 5d: an FPGA target naming
+`board.gptp_owner` is refused, so its gPTP owner stays the fabric plane
+(#259).
+
+**What differs.** These rows are the keys only the host profile reads, and
+the shared keys whose rule differs there. Gate 41 holds this table to the
+host loaders as gate 32 holds section 3 to the FPGA ones.
+
+| # | Key | On the host profile | Why |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 6a | `board.target` | `host`, outside `BOARDS` (`HOST_TARGET`) | no pin, clock or PHY table applies |
+| 6b | `board.gptp_owner` | required; `host-phc` is the only value | the board's own PHC owns gPTP time |
+| 6c | `board.constraints.link_mbps` | required, `100` or `1000` | SRP's class A ceiling (Milan v1.2 5.6); an FPGA board takes its rate from `BOARDS` |
+| 6d | `board.constraints.num_queues` | optional, default `5`, as row 5c | it bounds `srp.class_queue` |
+| 6e | `audio_interface.kind` | `usb_audio` alone (`HOST_INTERFACES`); its cluster label is `USB` | the board's media program's interface; the FPGA front-ends are refused there, and `usb_audio` is refused on an FPGA target |
+| 6f | `audio_interface.channels` | required, 1 to 32 | a USB Audio Class 2 function's width is configured, not a bus width |
+| 6g | `gptp.port_number` | required, 1 to 65534 | the port the board's gPTP program announces from; an FPGA target's is generator-owned (row 33b) |
+| 6h | `gptp.{priority1,priority2,clock_class,clock_accuracy,offset_scaled_log_variance,log_sync_interval,log_announce_interval,log_pdelay_interval}` | each required | the dataset that program announces, which AVB_INTERFACE repeats (IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.2.8); no engine supplies a pin (rows 31 and 32) |
+| 6i | `control.placement` | must be `split` | the host program is that firmware; `all-fabric` names the protocol processor |
+
+The host profile refuses `board.features` (it has no fabric blocks), the FPGA
+`board.constraints` keys, a `soc:` section, `gptp.ingress_latency_ns` and
+`gptp.egress_latency_ns` (the fabric plane's corrections, row 33d) and the
+`role-pools` cluster policy (its pilot and loopback pools are fabric sources).
+Two fabric derivations do not run there. The render-lane bound (#447) does
+not apply. SRP's TSpec takes no framer supply cap. Its channel width is the
+widest `channels_per_frame` any talker advertises among its formats
+(`framer_declared_channels`). Every talker row uses that one width at
+`clocking.sampling_rate_hz`. It is not each talker's current format. The
+reason is that IEEE 802.1Q-2018 35.2.2.8.4 a) makes MaxFrameSize "the maximum
+frame size that the Talker will produce", and here that is the widest
+advertised format. The control firmware declares one fixed TSpec per source.
+SET_STREAM_FORMAT moves an output that is not streaming to any format it
+advertises, and the declaration stays in place. MSRP changes no FirstValue of
+a declared StreamID short of a withdrawal and two LeaveAllTime periods
+(35.2.2.8). So a talker whose current format is narrower than another it
+advertises reserves for the wider one. Milan v1.2 4.3.3.2 Table 4.4 gives
+each format's value, and the profile takes the largest. Gate 41 holds this
+on a talker with a two-channel current format that also advertises eight
+channels: its MaxFrameSize is the eight-channel 217 octets, not the
+two-channel 73.
+
+**The station MAC.** The image bakes `platform.mac_address` and the
+mac-derived `entity_id` into three fields: ENTITY `entity_id`, AVB_INTERFACE
+`mac_address` and `clock_identity`. A board that reads its MAC at run time
+verifies the generated image against its CRC first, then substitutes its own
+MAC in those three fields. That step belongs to the board's integration, not
+to this repository.
+
+**The firmware shape.** THE SHAPES in
+[`ctrl_loop.h`](../sw/firmware/ctrl/loop/ctrl_loop.h) lists `(1, 1, 2)` for a
+build that defines `CTRL_HOST_PLATFORM`, and for no other. Its figures are
+1x1/1if's, held as a stated host scheduling profile rather than a
+measurement; its comment says what that profile claims and what it does not.
+Without the macro the shape is refused as before, and the macro moves no FPGA
+row. Gate 41 compiles all three cases. Gate 42 plants the refusals: a `board`
+that is not a mapping (an empty list, an empty string, a list naming a
+target), refused by `load_config`'s `ConfigError` before the profile is
+chosen, as it was before the host profile existed; the three ways an FPGA
+config still refuses a missing fabric gPTP owner; the host profile's own
+refusals; and the shared Milan and IEEE checks on the host example.
